TI  - AI-Augmented Blockchain Framework for Predictive Financial Analytics Using Federated Learning and Explainable AI
PY  - 2026
T2  - 2026 International Conference on Innovations in Engineering and Technology, ICIET 2026
DO  - 10.1109/ICIET70550.2026.11712633
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105054101344?origin=resultslist
AD  - M.Kumarasamy College of Engineering, Master of Business Administration, Tamil Nadu, Karur, India
AB  - The increase in digital financial transactions has increased the need to have intelligent systems of fraud detection, privacy-protective, and interpretable. Current centralized AI schemes have weaknesses of data privacy, a lack of transparency, and no audit trail of decisions, which restricts their application in controlled regulatory financial settings. An AI-Extended Blockchain Framework that combines Federated Learning, Transformer-based deep learning, SHAP-based Explainable AI, and Hyperledger Fabric permissioned blockchain to build predictive financial analytics. The federated learning engine employs weighted FedAvg aggregation across five non-IID institutional nodes, whereas the Transformer encoder facilitates intricate temporal transaction reliance through multi-head self-attention. SHAP attribution scores are intended to support transparent decision-making aligned with regulatory accountability expectations The proposed framework, when tested on the IEEE-CIS Fraud Detection Dataset, consisting of 590,540 transactions, has an F1-score of 95.75%, ROC-AUC of 0.9713, precision of 96.38%, and recall of 95.14% at federated round 15, showing competitive results with broader architectural coverage in privacy preservation, explainability, and blockchain-based auditability compared to current state-of-the-art baselines © 2026 IEEE.
