TI  - Integration of Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning into Wearable Health Technologies
PY  - 2025
T2  - Smart Textiles and Wearables for Health and Fitness
SP  - 137
EP  - 158
DO  - 10.1002/9781394302895.ch7
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105015780397?origin=resultslist
AD  - School of Computer Application, Lovely Professional University, Punjab, India
AB  - Wearable health technologies offer users more advanced and accurate health monitoring capabilities, giving priority to health-related functionalities. Wearable health technologies refer to electronic devices that individuals can wear or attach to their bodies to monitor various aspects of their health and well-being. Artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML) play a key role in enhancing the capabilities and effectiveness of wearable health solutions. The integration of AI and ML into wearable health technologies represents a paradigm shift in healthcare delivery, providing previously unknown possibilities for personalized monitoring, diagnosis, and treatment. This chapter commences with a discussion of the enhancing significance of wearable health technologies in advanced healthcare and highlights how they can be used to monitor physiological indicators continuously and unnoticeably such as activity levels and vital signs. The chapter then describes the key AI and ML methods used in wearable health solutions, such as predictive modeling, deep learning, and RL. It draws attention to their functions in data fusion, anomaly detection, and predictive analytics, demonstrating their capacity to diagnose early illness symptoms of diseases, tailor treatment plans, and enhance health outcomes in totality. Moreover, the chapter also discusses issues that arise when integrating AI and ML into wearable health technologies, including data protection, interoperability, and interpretability of algorithms. To solve these issues and realize the full promise of AI-driven wearable health technologies, it also looks at new trends including explainable AI, edge computing, and federated learning. At last, this chapter concludes by highlighting the revolutionary effects of integrating AI and ML into wearable health technologies, providing a research roadmap for the future, and emphasizing the enormous potential to transform healthcare delivery and enable people to take charge of their health and well-being.
