AB  - In the era of digital transformation, machine learning (ML) has become a key enabler of innovation in business models and decision-making frameworks. This conceptual paper adopts a literature review approach, complemented by cross-sectoral case illustrations, to assess the strategic role of ML in enhancing data-driven decision-making, operational efficiency, and customer-centric services across industries such as finance, healthcare, manufacturing, and retail. Organizations are shifting from descriptive analytics toward predictive and prescriptive models, using ML to automate processes, detect anomalies, personalize offerings, and deliver real-time insights that inform strategic actions. However, the integration of ML into enterprise systems presents several challenges, including data quality issues, limited computational infrastructure, algorithmic bias, ethical concerns, and the need for transparent and trustworthy decision-making. To address these challenges, this study proposes a structured ML adoption framework that emphasizes robust data governance, ethical and explainable AI, scalable infrastructure, and workforce readiness. The paper also explores the long-term trajectory of ML as a driver of sustainable innovation and competitive advantage. Through comprehensive analysis and practical recommendations, this study points out the revolutionary possibilities of ML and offers strategic guidance for organizations seeking to implement ML technologies responsibly and at scale in support of ongoing digital transformation. © 2026 The Author(s).
