AB  - Automated Grading Systems (AGS) play a central role in digitally transformed and data-driven higher education environments. Drawing on machine learning, natural language processing, and emerging generative models, AGS support scal-able, consistent, and timely evaluation of both structured and open-ended student work. When embedded within smart campus ecosystems, these systems interact with Learning Management Systems, Learning Record Stores, and analytics dashboards to enable real-time feedback, adaptive learning support, and informed programme-level decision-making. Their implementation enhances institutional efficiency and personalised learning pathways. However, challenges remain concerning algorithmic transparency, data governance, cultural and linguistic fairness, and the safeguarding of academic judgement. This chapter contends that the value of AGS lies not only in their computational capabilities, but in responsible governance frameworks that ensure equitable and pedagogically aligned assessment practices. © 2026 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
