AB  - Dual-purpose machine learning and deep learning applications in financial institutions have been rapidly adopted into the financial industry and have changed the way loans are approved and credit risks are evaluated. Even though these models have a better predictive power than the traditional statistical methods, their black-box character makes them questionable in terms of transparency, fairness, accountability, and compliance to regulations. Explainable Artificial Intelligence (XAI) has become a key paradigm to deal with these worries as it offers human-interpretable explanations regarding decision-making by a model. In this paper, the review of XAI methods used in loan approval and credit risk assessment has been done in detail. The review summarizes contemporary developments in explainable machine learning models, model-agnostic, model-specific explanation techniques, ensemble and hybrid techniques, privacy-preserving systems, and fairness-conscious systems. In addition, the main challenges, evaluation measures, and future research directions are also addressed, as XAI can be instrumental in creating trustworthy and ethical financial decision-support systems. © 2026 IEEE.
