AB  - By means of sophisticated, data-driven systems that improve patient care, diagnoses, and treatment techniques, artificial intelligence (AI) is redefining healthcare and transforming conventional medical procedures. Future developments in artificial intelligence that will change healthcare systems for the next generation are investigated in this work. Precision medicine driven by artificial intelligence, predictive analytics, and real-time monitoring is enhancing illness diagnosis, patient outcomes, and tailored treatments. Medical imaging is improving because to deep learning models and computer vision, which also allow early, more accurate disease identification. Furthermore boosting healthcare efficiency and lowering human workload are AI-powered robotic surgery and automation in administrative processes. Continuous health monitoring and preemptive interventions are made possible by the way artificial intelligence is being combined with wearable health devices and the Internet of Medical Things (IoMT). By means of virtual assistants and AI-driven chatbots, natural language processing and conversational artificial intelligence are enhancing patient involvement. Furthermore improving data security, interoperability, and privacy in digital health records is the mix of artificial intelligence and blockchain technology. Notwithstanding these developments, important issues including ethical questions, regulatory compliance, and the requirement of explainable artificial intelligence still exist. This paper addresses developing trends that will define the future of intelligent, efficient, and patient-centric healthcare systems as well as the transforming possibilities of artificial intelligence in healthcare. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2025.
