AB  - The expanding complexity of enterprise and healthcare data demands scalable ethical and interpretable AI-driven results. Standard predictive models don't have more transparency, hamper ethical compliance, and decline to adapt efficiently within cloud-native environments. To focus these restraints, this research proposes an Explainable AI (XAI)-driven Predictive Analytics Framework that incorporates hybrid CNN-Transformer architectures with SHAP and LIME-based interpretability layers. The study is proposed for continuous implementation in cloud-native architecture using a microservice-based architecture that guarantees real-time adaptability, robust data governance, interoperability Federated learning and differential privacy improve data security while preserving model generalization. Experimental evaluations on Kaggle's Diabetes Expectation and IBM HR Attrition datasets show better performance, achieving 97.8% accuracy, 97.0% F1-score, and 0.985 AUC. Compared to old models, the proposed framework advances superior interpretability, scalability, and ethical alignment, determining a widespread benchmark for visible automation in AI-driven decision approaches. © 2026 IEEE.
