AB  - This new and unprecedented proliferation of data from a variety of sources (cloud platforms, IoT devices, business applications, distributed databases) has created significant challenges in data governance, such as data quality management, security and privacy protection, regulatory compliance and scalable decision making. Traditional governance approaches are often inadequate to tackle the dynamic and complex nature of modern enterprise ecosystems. This paper introduces an AI-Driven Data Governance Framework for Enterprise Data Management which combines artificial intelligence, machine learning, and automated policy enforcement techniques to improve the efficiency, adaptability, and intelligence of data governance. The envisioned framework is to be implemented using intelligent data classification, anomaly detection, metadata management, predictive analytics, and automated compliance monitoring to preserve data integrity, transparency and reliability in enterprise environments. In addition, it also includes explainable AI mechanisms and role-based access control models that enhance trust, accountability, and security in enterprise data operations. Advanced analytics modules are used to help manage risks, monitor in real time and optimize governance while minimizing manual effort and overhead. It also enables scalable and resilient enterprise data management through interoperability on multi-cloud and hybrid infrastructures. The results of the experiments show that the proposed framework is more accurate in governance, efficient in compliance, accessible in data, and more efficient in operation than other traditional governance approaches. The findings underscore how AI governance systems can support next-generation digital enterprises to manage their enterprise data in an intelligent, secure, and sustainable manner. © 2026 IEEE.
