TI  - A Multimodal Foundation Model with Federated Temporal Graph Learning for Personalized Cardiovascular Risk Prediction
PY  - 2026
T2  - 6th International Conference on Inventive Computation and Information Technologies, ICICIT 2026 - Proceedings
SP  - 1557
EP  - 1563
DO  - 10.1109/ICICIT69063.2026.11634092
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105047886987?origin=resultslist
AD  - Saveetha Institute of Medical and Technical Sciences, Saveetha School of Engineering, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Chennai, India
AB  - Cardiovascular diseases are among the leading causes of humanity global, thus there is a necessity of more accurate and early predictive systems utilizing longitudinal healthcare data. The presented paper suggests Deep Cardio Sense++, a modern hybrid model of heart disease prediction based on Electronic Health Records using the MIMIC-III dataset. The model employs a Temporal Fusion Transformer to learn temporal relationships, a Graph Attention Network to learn the inter-patient relationships and a Federation Learning architecture to make sure that the training is distributed in a privacy-preserving manner. Furthermore, explainable AI methods like SHAP and attention mechanisms are implemented to increase the interpretability of the model. The experimental outcomes prove that the proposed framework is more accurate and has a higher precision, recall, and AUC-ROC when compared to the baseline models (98.4%). The results affirm that temporal, relational and privacy-conscious learning combined with one another is more beneficial to predictive performance and scalability. The suggested system provides a dependable and interpretable clinical solution to the real-world cardiovascular risk prediction tasks and decision support. © 2026 IEEE.
