AB  - AI is drastically changing the HRM practices by increasing competencies, decreasing biases and improving the capability of decision making. This study examines how AI is revolutionizing HR tasks by predictive analytics algorithms, chatbots and machine learning which are being incorporated into HR system to facilitate talent management, efficient workforce planning and streamlined administrative procedures. Automating the hiring processes, improving the candidate experience and encouraging employee collaboration through intelligent platforms. The possible drawbacks such as data privacy concern, algorithmic transparency, and moral issues with employee monitoring and decision making are also considered. The study includes Bibliometric Analysis using Vos-Viewer and 64 documents were used to evaluate the citation, keywords and co- authorship maps using Scopus database. The keywords for the search of data used were- Artificial Intelligence and Recruitment Process. The most common research themes are real time data validation, and use of AI in recruitment efficiency. © 2026, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
