TI  - Proposed Multi Model Agentic AI Architecture of Decision Support System for Corporate Leaders
PY  - 2026
T2  - 2026 International Conference on Emerging Technologies and Future Innovations, ETFI 2026
DO  - 10.1109/ETFI68128.2026.11484093
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105040768577?origin=resultslist
AD  - Des Pune University Pune, Pune, India
AB  - Corporate leaders today are expected to make fast, high stakes & Informed decisions backed by solid evidence, data driven and defendable reasoning. Yet most existing AIdriven decision tools operate like black boxes, offering conclusions without transparency or accountability. When a single model is forced to handle everything from forecasting to compliance analysis, results often become unstable, difficult to justify and risky to trust. This leads to hesitation, slow decision cycles and delayed or no AI adoption in practical corporate environments. This paper presents a multi-model agentic AI architecture built to support strategic decisions with clarity, traceability and confidence. The system uses iterative reasoning, hybrid evidence retrieval, adaptive model selection and explainable narrative outputs, all governed by a Trust, Risk and Security Management audit framework. It behaves less like an automated tool and more like a panel of expert advisors or Consultants who validate assumptions, compare perspectives and clearly show how a conclusion was reached. A real business evaluation conducted with FieldMI Technologies Pvt. Ltd. establishes the practical applicability in the corporate scenario. Using Sequential Prompt based decision support exercise with structured multi step reasoning methodology, the exercise delivered a decision confidence and projected forecasting simulation for stronger financial projections for a channel partner led first strategy. The result shows proposed multi-model agentic AI system can strengthen leadership conviction, mitigate risk and enhance decision quality. This research determines a foundation for Corporate Decision Support Systems (DSS) for Leaders, which is reliable, interpretable and ready for regulated corporate environments. It has possibility for future area of enhancement in autonomous learning and multi-model reasoning. © 2026 IEEE.
