AB  - AI as a game-changer in personalized medicine. This paper examines the transformative role of AI in optimizing drug discovery, treatment selection, and clinical decision-making. Machine learning and deep learning models trained on multi-omics data, electronic health records (EHRs), and real-world patient responses to drug treatment were developed to improve the predictive accuracy of disease progression, drug efficacy, and adverse event mitigation. AI-assisted drug repurposing and pharmacogenomic modelling predicts optimal therapy for each tumour so that patients get what will work for them the first time without the trial-and-error of prescriptions. Explainable AI (XAI) in decision support systems enhances model interpretability and promotes clinician trust. Convolutional and recurrent neural networks: Adaptive patient-specific treatments are enabled by reinforcement learning and deep neural networks It critically examines challenges such as data privacy, algorithmic bias, and regulatory compliance. We highlight the upcoming directions like federated learning, digital twin simulations, and quantum computing integration to make this AI-driven personalized medicine to come true. This paper presents a framework to operationalize artificial intelligence in healthcare – one which connects computational intelligence with precision medicine. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2026.
