UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105037607206?origin=resultslist
AD  - Universitas Padjadjaran, Faculty of Dentistry, Bandung, Indonesia
AD  - School of Electrical Engineering and Informatics, Institut Teknologi Bandung, Bandung, Indonesia
AB  - Ensuring service quality and satisfaction in public healthcare remains challenging due to limited resources and fragmented data utilization. This study proposes an AI-Enhanced Total Quality Management (TQM) framework that integrates Generative Artificial Intelligence (GenAI) and Explainable AI (XAI) to support predictive and evidence-based quality improvement. Using an exploratory sequential mixed-methods design, qualitative insights on organizational readiness and ethics were combined with quantitative survey data and machine learning models. Synthetic data generated via GANs were employed for privacy-preserving analytics, while Random Forest, XGBoost, and Artificial Neural Networks were evaluated using cross-validation and statistical significance testing. Results from a public dental hospital case study show that XGBoost achieved the highest predictive performance, and explainability analysis highlights leadership commitment and employee involvement as key determinants of satisfaction. The findings demonstrate that integrating GenAI and XAI into TQM enables transparent, data-driven, and human-centered quality governance in public healthcare. © 2026 IEEE.
