AD  - Walmart Global Tech, Sunnyvale, United States
AB  - Modern e-commerce thrives on interactive digital channels and virtual communities, with advances in social computing, data mining, and generative AI unlocking new opportunities for customer acquisition, retention, and platform resilience. This paper proposes a cross-platform framework that transforms passive clicks into active community engagement and buying intent. The system integrates generative AI for hyper-personalized content creation, recommendations, and sentiment-aware interactions; predictive data mining for trend discovery, churn prediction, and inventory optimization; and social computing for uncovering behavioral patterns and fostering digital communities. Grounded in recent studies (2020-2025), the framework demonstrates significant impact: more than 30% improvements in loyalty and repeat purchases, conversion rates up to four times higher, and buyer journeys accelerated by nearly 50% compared to conventional digital models. The architecture also incorporates privacy-by-design, explainable AI, and scalable cloud-native deployment to mitigate challenges in trust, ethics, and system performance. Findings provide both a theoretical foundation and a practical roadmap for integrating AI-driven personalization and community building in e-commerce, offering value to researchers, practitioners, and policymakers pursuing sustainable digital innovation.  © 2025 IEEE.
