AB  - Artificial intelligence (AI) is revolutionizing the health sector due to fast diagnosis, individualized management, Toral functions, cost-savings, patient care, and organizational performance. The importance is based on the fact that it can close the gap between the technology and its real use in the clinical workflow. For this reason, all healthcare providers are either unwilling to rely on such AI models in some severe circumstances, as many of them are challenging to understand. The integration of AI technology in the hospitals show that there are no well-defined rules and standards on the use of the technology. All these are to be kept in consideration in order to get maximum benefits of AI in healthcare to avoid any aspect of being risky, wrong, or unethical. The reason for the chapter is to allow the care practitioners and the researchers to know what is needed when applying AI in healthcare, which can easily allow the integration of the advancement in practice, if the difficulties that may include the ethical issues, data privacy, as well as compatibility with other already present systems in the healthcare facilities are fixed. It is important to compare all different AI models to get to the conclusion of efficiency, accuracy, and what could be an issue in clinical environment. Data privacy and ethical issues are also addressed on the primary focus when it comes to envisaging the prospective impact of AI-based healthcare solutions. In terms of challenges, the key ones are the data privacy, the lack of clear regulations, and potentially bias in some AI models regarding their usage in the healthcare sector to the full extent possible. That is why it is the integration of such technology into healthcare with such great potential that is only possible where the issues of ethical guidelines and validation are critical factors for success. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
