AB  - Today in the era of Artificial Intelligence (AI) where datasets in a large scale need to be processed for data processing. We require cloud technology to handle such dataset. AI with cloud computing together provide optimized usage of autonomous systems, security improvements, and intelligent resource management. This work mainly focuses on the interdependence and its impact on health care services. Here case-based approach across five applications of Cloud AI (medical imaging diagnostics, predictive patient analytics, drug discovery, telemedicine, and operations optimization) is considered. Furthermore, there are significant challenges, including data privacy and security relating issues are addressed. In this paper we examined these challenges in detail and made recommendations to mitigate them. Lastly, we also explored emerging frontiers viz. Federated Learning (FL) for collaborative training while preserving privacy, Edge-Cloud hybrid systems for low-latency services, and the combination of Explainable AI (XAI) with blockchain to provide an auditable and transparent data-aggregation system. © 2026 IEEE.
