AB  - Digital government transformation creates integrated public service ecosystems but simultaneously generates system fragmentation, application duplication, and systemic technological risks. Traditional periodic, sample-based, organization-oriented technology audits are inadequate for addressing these challenges. This chapter proposes a layered smart technology audit framework for national digital government ecosystems combining regulations, standardized audit tools, artificial intelligence,andcontinuousauditingprinciples.WithintheIndonesianpolicycontext (SPBE and BRIN technology audit regulations), this framework positions auditing as knowledge infrastructure and governance intelligence supporting regulatory assurance, predictive risk management, and strategic public service interoperability strengthening. AI techniques—machine learning, predictive analytics, natural language processing, and explainable AI—enable full population analysis, near real-time risk detection, and evidence-based policy insights at national scales. Copyright © 2027, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. Copying or distributing in print or electronic forms without written permission of IGI Global Scientific Publishing is prohibited. Use of this chapter to train generative artificial intelligence (AI) technologies is expressly prohibited. The publisher reserves all rights to license its use for generative AI training and machine learning model development.
