AB  - With the rapid advancement of big data, cloud computing, and artificial intelligence, governments worldwide are undergoing a profound transformation in policy decision-making. This paper systematically examines the role and implementation of AI-driven Public Policy Decision Support Systems (PPDSS). Firstly, the paper defines PPDSS and outlines the core AI technologies that underpin these systems, including natural language processing, machine learning, computer vision, and reinforcement learning. Secondly, it explores major application areas, demonstrating how PPDSS enable intelligent policy analysis, real-time public opinion monitoring, predictive risk assessment, and optimized crisis management. The paper then establishes a dynamic closed-loop model of “data collection-intelligent analysis-decision support-effect evaluation,” illustrating the shift in public governance from an experience-based paradigm to a data-driven, intelligent one. Furthermore, the paper identifies and analyzes critical challenges in implementation, such as data quality, algorithmic transparency, organizational capacity, and ethical governance. In conclusion, future research directions are proposed, emphasizing the need for cross-domain data fusion, enhanced human-AI collaboration, and robust algorithmic accountability to foster more scientific, transparent, and responsive policymaking. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
