AB  - The explosive nature of data in dispersed enterprise environments has put pressure on the requirement to have a strong, scaled, and intelligent data governance systems. Conventional data governance frameworks tend to be based on fixed rule-based system that does not have dynamism, scalability, and real-time decision-making in a dynamic data ecosystem. The data governance model suggested in this paper combines machine learning, natural language processing, and policy enforcement to improve the data quality, security, compliance, and lifecycle management through the use of AI. The suggested framework builds on the use of smart data classification, anomaly detection, and predictive analytics to allow proactive governance and risk mitigation. Moreover, explainable AI methods are also included in the model to maintain transparency and accountability in automated decisions in governance, which aligns with regulatory standards (e.g., GDPR or enterprise compliance standards). There is the introduction of a multi-layered architecture consisting of data ingestion, semantic enrichment, policy intelligence, and governance orchestration layers to allow integration of heterogeneous data sources such as cloud, edge and on-premise systems, seamlessly. Experimental assessment indicates that there are major gains in data accuracy, policy compliance, and operational efficiency in contrast to conventional methods of governance. The findings point to the potentials of AI-based governance models in changing the concept of data management by allowing organizations to attain intelligent, autonomous, and scalable data governance in the contemporary data-driven environments.  © 2026 IEEE.
