AB  - In this paper, a neuro-symbolic agentic architecture of personalized financial decision support is proposed combining deterministic financial logic and generative reasoning. The system combines supervised machine learning models of goal classification and risk prediction with a controlled Large Language Model (LLM) to produce explanations. Synthetic data analysis has 89% and 85% accuracy on financial goal classification and risk appetite prediction respectively and good precision, recall and ROC-AUC. The architecture allows interpretability, auditability, and controlled reasoning and breaks significant weaknesses of the purely generative or purely rule-based systems. The suggested system stands a great chance of intelligent financial advisory systems that are accurate and scalable. © 2026 IEEE.
