AB  - Neurodegenerative disorders (NDDs) are a significant health problem all over the world. These include Alzheimer's disease, Parkinson's disease, Huntington's disease and amyotrophic lateral sclerosis. This chapter provides a review of the present state of predictive analytics when detecting NDDs at their early stages. It includes the basic modeling methods, the progress in the multimodal data integration, the practical constraints and the prospects of the future. To minimize NDDs with the help of predictive analytics, an adequate framework is necessary that would transform various biomedical data into practical clinical conclusions. This model usually entails four major steps, which include data acquisition; data preprocessing and feature engineering; model development; and clinical integration and decision support. Emerging trends and methodological advances include multimodal data fusion, longitudinal modeling, deep learning and advanced artificial intelligence (AI) techniques, explainable AI, federated learning and data privacy, and real-world digital health integration. © ISTE Ltd 2026.
