TI  - An Explainable AI Framework for Digital Intake and Pre-Visit Workflow Optimization in Interoperable EHR Ecosystems
PY  - 2026
T2  - 2026  3rd Technology and Innovation Conference, TIC 2026
DO  - 10.1109/TIC68483.2026.11702869
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105055248308?origin=resultslist
AD  - Windermere, Florida, 34786, United States
AB  - Digital patient intake and pre-visit workflows are the critical first touchpoints in healthcare delivery, yet their integration with Electronic Health Record (EHR) systems is often ad hoc. The article proposes a framework for explainable artificial intelligence (XAI) that aims to enhance digital intake by structurally harmonizing data, prioritizing cases based on risks, and generating recommendations transparently for pre-visit planning. The assessment is based on operational and model centered performance measures, such as the percentage of patients completing intake, the number of errors in documentation, the average pre-visit processing time, the accuracy of triage, F1-score, the area under the receiver operating characteristic curve (AUC-ROC), as well as explainability utility measured through user agreement and the rate of action acceptance. Experimental data reveal that the developed model is very efficient and performs well with the baseline rule based workflows as it not only improves throughput but also provides more reliable predictions and significantly increases human trust in recommendations. By capturing and integrating different stakeholders' processes in a human centered fashion, this research work is a demonstration that making XAI and interoperable is not a theoretical exercise: it has the potential to substantially increase physician efficiency in pre-visit tasks, while the accountability and clinical usability are kept intact. © 2026 IEEE.
