AB  - The proceedings contain 17 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Information and Communication. The topics include: Automated Detection of Acceptive and Dismissive Dialogue Acts: A Synthetic LLM-Based Dataset and a SetFit Classification Model; bridging Communication Gaps: A Real-Time Sign Language Recognition and Audio-Text Conversion System; Agile Digital Government in Data Governance: An Assessment of the Jambi Data Analysis Center (JDAC) in Jambi Province Government; a Voice-Driven Framework for Web Navigation: Enhancing Accessibility for Visually Impaired Users Through Natural Language Processing; A Comprehensive Benchmarking of Explainable AI Techniques on Camel Type Dataset; AI-Augmented IoT Architecture for Automated Attendance Using RFID and Facial Biometrics with Enhanced Security and Integration; Ontology for AI Music Generation Tools; experimental Evaluation of Organ Tracking Accuracy in Depth–Depth Matching for Combined Parallel and Rotational Movements When Sensor Mounting Causes Error; heterogeneous IoT Device Integration Through a Digital Twin Framework and Adopting the Reactive Programming Paradigm; google-MedGemma Based Abnormality Detection in Musculoskeletal Radiographs; A Lightweight Hybrid Encryption Model for Secure EHR in IoT Environments; the Innovation of Medical Diagnostic Technology: A Case Study on Stroke Diagnostics; Novel Architecture of RPA in Oral Cancer Lesion Detection; Linking the Scales with AI: How Local Processes Determine Success of Large-Scale Nature-Based Solutions; a Comparative Study of Stress and Its Effect on Work Performance of Female Employees in Higher Education Institutions in Rural and Metropolitan Areas, with Special Reference to Wardha and Nagpur Districts; advanced Anomaly Detection Techniques for Water Quality Monitoring: Implementation and Evaluation Using Physicochemical Datasets; the Impact of Immersive Digital Twins on Industrial Process Optimization: An Exploratory Study.
