AD  - Karunya Institute of Tech. and Sci., School of CST, Coimbatore, India
AB  - Smallholder farms require trustworthy, low cost decision support that works with limited bandwidth and strict privacy needs. Centralized training risks data leakage and often misses locality specific patterns, while purely edge training fragments knowledge and weakens calibration and interpretability. This paper presents FedEdge X, a secure and explainable federated edge AI framework that keeps raw data on device, applies differentially private local training with secure aggregation, and pairs domain aware augmentation with post training calibration. A compact multimodal model processes RGB images, IoT time series, and tabular weather to support disease recognition, irrigation advisory, soil moisture forecasting, and yield prediction. Evaluation on IFD Fields (18k/2k/2.5k), OPD Plant (12.5k/1.5k/2k), SoilSense (2.6M/0.3M/0.3M points), Irrigo (45k/5k/5k), and YieldTrack (9.6k/1.2k/1.2k) shows that FedEdge X improves classification over strong baselines on IFD (95.3 accuracy, 94.8 F1) and OPD (96.4, 95.9), and on irrigation (92.6, 92.1), while reducing soil moisture error to 3.41 RMSE and 11.1 MAPE and yield error to 0.56 t/ha RMSE and 9.5 MAPE. On Raspberry Pi class hardware the framework achieves 45.9 ms latency and 21.8 FPS, with an INT8 variant reaching 39.2 ms and 25.5 FPS. These results indicate that privacy preserving federation with calibrated probabilities and lightweight explanations can deliver reliable, field ready intelligence for climate smart smallholder farming. © 2026 IEEE.
