TI  - An Explainable Human-in-the-Loop Agentic AI Framework for Continuous Financial Planning and Analysis Beyond Forecast Accuracy
PY  - 2026
T2  - International Conference on Multidisciplinary Innovations for Smart and Sustainable Future, MISSF 2026: Innovations Driving a Sustainable and Intelligent Future
DO  - 10.1109/MISSF68264.2026.11522093
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105041821097?origin=resultslist
AD  - SMTS, Westfield, IN, United States
AB  - Recent developments in artificial intelligence have enhanced the accuracy of financial forecasting, but most Financial Planning and Analysis (FP&A) studies have been preoccupied with predictive AI-powered decision systems design as opposed to the reliability of AI-powered forecasting. The missing element in real research relates to the lack of an AInative architecture of the full FP&A process that would consolidate uncertainty-aware predictive acts, explainable predictive reasoning, and operational responsibility, along with human governance. This paper suggests an Explainable Human-in-the-Loop Agentic AI model making FP&A not a one-off forecasting exercise, but an ongoing, AI-aided decision-making process. It has a combination of the probabilistic forecasting modules that are coupled with the explainable AI modules, multi agent workflow orchestration and structured human approval points to support transparency and accountable financial decision making. Autonomous agents implement the data ingestion coordination, and scenario simulation and budget optimization workloads and ensure auditability and compliance throughout the planning lifecycle by maintaining integrated governance layers. In contrast to the conventional methods that engage in the assessment of success based on accuracy of prediction, the suggested framework proposes decision adoption measures to determine whether AI-powered insights are accepted and used by the leaders of the financial industry. The architecture thus strives to bring FP&A to a scalable, interpretable, and governable AI ecosystem with the power to enable planning, budgeting, and strategic reforecasting on an ongoing basis.  © 2026 IEEE.
