AB  - About one in six people worldwide are affected by infertility, fostering a deepened reliance on assisted reproductive technologies (ARTs) like in vitro fertilization (IVF). However, the standard IVF decision-making process often does not include a structured assessment of mitochondrial risks that affect oocyte quality, treatment planning, and qualification for procedures like mitochondrial replacement therapy (MRT). The described system is an AI-driven clinical decision support system (CDSS) that encompasses patient assessment, oocyte mitochondrial health assessment, donor screening and recommendation, and explainable AI. The system performs machine-learning-based triage to select patients who may benefit from a targeted mitochondrial evaluation and builds support for donor compatibility decisions, utilizing both rule-based and data-driven approaches. Explainability has been ingrained through SHAP-based feature attributions to enable clinician trust and auditability. While the full mitochondrial imaging analysis module (CNN-based oocyte morphology assessment) remains future work since data were not available, the actualized modules build an operational decision support pipeline. Results from synthetic datasets show strong calibration, discriminative ability, and interpretable outputs that are amenable to further clinical validation. © 2026 IEEE.
