AB  - Artificial intelligence (AI) is transforming patient recruitment and retention in clinical trials by addressing the inefficiencies in traditional methods. This study conducts a secondary literature review and comparative analysis to evaluate AI-driven strategies such as machine learning, natural language processing, AI-powered clinical decision support tools, generative AI, etc. Key findings suggest that AI enhances patient identification, eligibility screening, and engagement strategies, leading to faster recruitment and improved retention rates. Furthermore, the comparative analyses conducted in our study demonstrate AI’s superiority over conventional recruitment approaches, while the industry case studies highlight its real-world impact and potential applications. However, challenges such as selection bias, data privacy concerns, and AI explainability remain significant barriers to adopting AI in patient recruitment and retention in clinical trials that must be addressed. We also explore the possibility of certain emerging technological advancements as potential pathways for AI in future clinical research. Nonetheless, further research should focus on aspects such as ethical AI implementation, fairness in patient selection, and regulatory frameworks to optimize AI-driven clinical trial recruitment and retention. © ICST Institute for Computer Sciences, Social Informatics and Telecommunications Engineering 2027.
