AB  - This chapter explores the evolution and application of algorithmic thinking and artificial intelligence (AI) in healthcare. Tracing historical roots from antiquity to modern quantum computing, it demonstrates how algorithmic logic has shaped clinical diagnostics, treatment, and healthcare systems. Emphasis is placed on AI’s transformative impact, which enhances diagnostic accuracy, personalizes treatments, optimizes hospital resource allocation, and enables real-time patient monitoring. Key technologies include deep learning, reinforcement learning, and electronic health records, all of which support predictive analytics and clinical decision-making. The chapter also critically examines ethical dilemmas, including algorithmic bias, data privacy, explainability, and accountability. Emerging approaches, such as Explainable AI (XAI) and AI governance frameworks, are discussed as solutions to transparency and trust issues. Ultimately, the chapter advocates for interdisciplinary collaboration and robust regulation to ensure the equitable, secure, and effective integration of AI into healthcare. © 2026 Marjo Rissanen, Kalle Saastamoinen and Tuija S. Ikonen.
