AB  - Cloud Computing intersecting with Artificial Intelligence (AI) is changing digital ecosystems with intelligent, autonomous and scalable services. The present paper will provide an overview of the recent progress in AI-driven cloud platforms with a particular focus on predictive analytics, anomaly detection, dynamic resource management, and edge + cloud collaboration. Although the technologies enhance efficiency, security, and realtime decision-making there are a few challenges such as scaling of AI models, data privacy, cross-heterogeneous platforms, and ultra-low latency that exist. A conceptual framework to solve these problems is suggested, which incorporates sustainable computing practices, explainable and energy-efficient models of AI, and adaptive orchestration. The paper identifies the prospects of AIbased cloud infrastructures to design resilient, secure, and sustainable digital ecosystems that can have powerful applications in healthcare, finance, smart cities, and industrial automation.  © 2025 IEEE.
