AB  - The increasing frequency and intensity of natural disasters reveal critical gaps in early warning, preparedness, and coordinated response. This paper presents an AI-powered, multi-hazard alerting system designed to predict and manage disasters such as wildfires, floods, and earthquakes using machine learning models trained on real-time and historical data. The system employs ensemble learning strategies, including XGBoost, LSTM, and SVM, to deliver geo-localized, tiered alerts to public safety agencies, insurers, and individuals. A case study on the 2018 Camp Fire in California illustrates the potential benefits of the system in improving evacuation timing, public communication, and financial risk modeling. The framework also addresses legal and ethical considerations, such as data governance, algorithmic transparency, and liability management. This work bridges artificial intelligence with public policy and industry resilience, offering a scalable and ethically aligned platform for disaster risk management. © 2025 IEEE.
