AB  - The use of predictive modelling as a key strategy to help the world reach the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) has changed finance forever. Predictive models help measure sustainability-based goals more accurately, keep track of progress more efficiently, and speed up the process of evaluating progress by using advanced statistical analysis, machine learning algorithms, and financial risk analysis. This article outlines an implementation framework that connects financial data with sustainability metrics. It focusses on data collection, preprocessing, feature engineering, model building, validation, and integrating decision systems. The study underscores that predictive modelling increases transparency in financial reporting, facilitates evidence-based policy interventions, and improves accountability in resource allocation for sustainable investments. The proposed framework demonstrates how predictive systems can align financial decision-making with SDG objectives; however, it also highlights considerable challenges, including data heterogeneity, model interpretability, and governance constraints. The study suggests that the achievement of future interoperability through technologies such as explainable artificial intelligence (XAI), blockchain, and federated learning could significantly enhance the scalability, security, and ethical implementation of predictive models. In short, the paper advocates for the advancement of sustainable finance by presenting predictive modelling as a catalyst for quantitative and accountable global progress. © 2025 IEEE.
