AB  - Hazardous industries such as construction report high accident rates, where non-compliance with Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) is a significant contributing factor. While AI-powered computer vision systems are increasingly used for automated monitoring, their "black box"nature often impedes trust, user adoption, and accountability. This paper proposes a novel conceptual framework, X-RF-DETR, designed to provide not only accurate but also explainable and trustworthy real-time PPE compliance monitoring to aid decision-making in occupational health and safety (OHS). The proposed framework integrates the RF-DETR Transformer-based detector with a dedicated Explainable AI (XAI) module. This module generates visual evidence to explain the model's detection results, thereby enhancing transparency and interpretability. Although conceptual, the framework's feasibility is supported by a proposed validation plan using public PPE data and standard explainability metrics. The primary contribution is the synthesis of a high-performance detection model with an XAI layer to address the critical gap of trustworthiness in AI safety systems, aligning with AI risk management standards like ISO/IEC 23894:2023. Ultimately, the X-RF-DETR framework promises to enhance human-AI collaboration, facilitate more informed decisions for safety managers, and increase the acceptance of automated monitoring technologies in high-risk environments. © 2025 IEEE.
