AB  - Land and maritime border management in Europe faces growing challenges, with rising traffic volumes, unpredictable flows, and the need to balance security with traveller convenience. Existing solutions, such as kiosks and through-window biometrics, remain limited in efficiency, scalability, and societal acceptance. This vision paper presents AutoBorder, a next-generation approach to border control that proposes seamless drive-through checks for both commercial and passenger vehicles. The system concept integrates in-vehicle sensing, Digital Travel Credentials (DTCs), advanced risk assessment with explainable AI (XAI), and privacy-by-design principles into a unified, modular architecture. AutoBorder introduces a layered system design covering traveller pre-registration, secure data transmission, in-vehicle identification, and decision support for border guards, built to interoperate with existing EU border systems. The approach addresses the diverse needs of multiple stakeholders: travellers seeking convenience, border authorities and infrastructure operators requiring efficiency, law enforcement agencies aiming to strengthen security, and the automotive industry exploring new integration opportunities. To validate this vision, pilot trials are foreseen across freight vehicles, coaches, and passenger cars at selected land and maritime borders, assessing adaptability and real-world feasibility. By tackling delays, enhancing trust, and embedding safeguards for fundamental rights, AutoBorder offers a forward-looking blueprint for efficient, secure, and human-centric border management. © 2025 IEEE.
