AB  - This chapter examines the future directions and responsible deployment of artificial intelligence (AI) for social impact within humanitarian contexts. This chapter emphasizes the transformative potential of AI in enhancing decision support systems, developing explainable AI (XAI) techniques, addressing climate-related challenges, and encouraging cross-sector partnerships. The chapter outlines essential future research directions, including ethical and governance frameworks, human-AI collaboration, AI-driven healthcare solutions, data integration and interoperability, context-aware AI systems, community engagement, and long-term impact assessment. This chapter also presents the action points focusing on establishing ethical guidelines, promoting cross-sector collaboration, prioritizing community needs, investing in innovation, and advocating for responsible AI practices. This chapter emphasizes the critical need for transparency, accountability, and ethical considerations in AI deployment, aiming to harness AI’s capabilities to build resilient, sustainable, and inclusive humanitarian systems. The authors posit that by leveraging AI responsibly, stakeholders can enhance the efficiency, effectiveness, and equity of humanitarian efforts, ultimately contributing to a more just and equitable world. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Adeyemi Abel Ajibesin and Narasimha Rao Vajjhala; individual chapters, the contributors.
