AD  - Shivaji University, Computer Science and Technology, Department of Technology, Maharashtra, Kolhapur, India
AB  - Thyroid disorders and Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS) are widespread hormonal conditions that share similar symptoms, often leading to delayed or inaccurate diagnosis. This study introduces a Hybrid AI Diagnostic Framework that combines Machine Learning (ML), Deep Learning (DL), Federated Learning (FL), and Explainable AI (XAI) to enhance diagnostic accuracy while ensuring privacy and transparency. The main objective is to review and analyze current AI-based diagnostic approaches and demonstrate how hybrid models improve detection efficiency. The reviewed literature shows that such systems achieve around 10-15% higher diagnostic accuracy compared with conventional single-model methods, mainly due to their ability to process multi-type medical data, including clinical, biochemical, and imaging information. The novelty of the proposed framework lies in integrating privacy-preserving federated training with explainable decision support, allowing clinicians to interpret model outputs with confidence. Overall, the findings highlight that hybrid AI models provide a practical, secure, and interpretable solution for early diagnosis of thyroid disorders and PCOS, contributing to more reliable and patient entered healthcare. © 2025 IEEE.
