TI  - AI-BASED DECISION SUPPORT SYSTEMS AND LEADERSHIP EFFECTIVENESS IN COMPLEX PROJECTS: THE EFFECTIVENESS OF AI-BASED DECISION SUPPORT SYSTEMS IN ENHANCING LEADERSHIP EFFECTIVENESS
PY  - 2025
T2  - Proceedings of the 2025 International Annual Conference and 46th Annual Meeting: Powering the Future of Engineering Management, ASEM 2025
SP  - 243
EP  - 250
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105035387011?origin=resultslist
AD  - Western Michigan University, United States
AB  - This paper examines the impact of AI-based Decision Support Systems (DSS) on leadership effectiveness in managing complex projects. By analyzing case studies from industries such as construction, healthcare, and software development, the study identifies key factors for successful AI-based DSS integration. The findings highlight several benefits of AI-based DSS, including real-time insights, resource optimization, and strategic planning. These systems are compared to traditional decision-making methods, demonstrating their advantages in speed, accuracy, and data-driven optimization. However, the study also addresses ethical concerns such as AI bias, transparency, and data privacy. Leadership effectiveness is assessed using the Essential Behavioral Leadership Qualities (EBLQ) framework, which evaluates leaders based on standardized behavioral attributes. This study emphasizes the importance of technological infrastructure, organizational readiness, and leadership support for the successful integration of AI-based DSS. It also discusses the challenges of data quality, algorithmic transparency, and adaptability to dynamic environments. The paper offers recommendations for overcoming barriers to AI adoption and ensuring responsible AI implementation. By enhancing understanding of AI's role in leadership, this research provides practical guidance for leveraging AI in complex projects. Future research directions include assessing the long-term impact of AI-based DSS on leadership development, exploring ethical AI frameworks, and developing strategies to enhance human-AI collaboration in project management. © American Society for Engineering Management, 2025.
