AB  - This paper explores the intersection of artificial intelligence (AI) and technology management, elucidating how their integration can foster competitive advantage and foster a culture of continuous innovation within organizations. Through a comprehensive review of literature, the transformative impacts of AI on technology management are analyzed, focusing on key areas such as strategic decision-making, capacity planning, communication, and risk management. The study highlights the potential of AI-driven forecasting models to optimize inventory management and supply chain processes, enhance network security, and streamline maintenance procedures. However, the integration of AI applications with existing business processes presents various challenges, including the need for robust change management strategies, effective security policies, and solutions to address the lack of algorithmic transparency. By strategically navigating these challenges and leveraging AI technologies, organizations can unlock new opportunities, enhance operational efficiency, and achieve sustainable growth in today׳s dynamic business landscape. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies.
