AD  - Saveetha School of Engineering, Saveetha Institute of Medical and Technical Sciences, Saveetha University (SIMATS), Department of Electronics and Communication Engineering, Tamil Nadu, Chennai, India
AB  - Federated Learning (FL) is ideal for delicate healthcare applications since it allows for cross-institutional collaborative model training without exposing raw patient data. Nevertheless, federated models frequently hinder clinical confidence and acceptance because to their opacity. This research presents a paradigm for blockchain-coordinated FL in cervical cancer risk prediction using explainable AI (XAI). The framework uses XGBoost and Logistic Regression in a privacy-preserving FL setting. To derive interpretable, case-specific explanations without disclosing raw data, it uses SHAP (SHapley Additive Explanations) and LIME (Local Interpretable Model-agnostic Explanations). By identifying critical risk factors, such as age and the number of sexual partners, therapists can have a better understanding of the model's decisions. The suggested method guarantees confidentiality, transparency, and clinical application while achieving high predictive accuracy, according to the experimental results. The approach demonstrates how real-world healthcare systems can benefit from federated learning that is both secure and easy to understand.  © 2025 IEEE.
