AB  - This study synthesizes the current state of research on the application of artificial intelligence (AI) in business decision-making contexts. A comprehensive search strategy was employed to identify relevant studies published between 2015 and 2024. Findings reveal a diverse range of AI applications, including predictive analytics, natural language processing, and recommendation systems, across various business functions such as finance, marketing, and supply chain management. Machine learning algorithms, particularly deep learning, were prominently featured in the literature. Reported benefits of AI adoption include improved decision accuracy, efficiency gains, and enhanced strategic insights, while challenges such as data privacy concerns, algorithmic bias, and organizational resistance were also identified. Furthermore, emerging trends such as explainable AI and human-AI collaboration present opportunities for advancing the field. This review contributes to a comprehensive understanding of the landscape of AI in business decision-making and offers insights for researchers, practitioners, and policymakers seeking to harness the potential of AI in driving organizational success. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2024.
